module

public import StacksFrontier.CategoryTheory.Sites.Simplicial.SliceAbelianLowerShriekFreeYoneda
public import StacksFrontier.CategoryTheory.Sites.Simplicial.SliceFreeAbelianLowerShriekNaturality

/-!
# Stacks 0D87 part (2) on free abelian sheaves, natural in `L`, at any spelling of the topology

`StacksFrontier/CategoryTheory/Sites/Simplicial/SliceFreeAbelianLowerShriekNaturality.lean` proves
that the shriek restriction transition `j_{M!}j_M^{-1} ⟶ j_{N!}j_N^{-1}` on free abelian sheaves
is carried to the set-level one, with the two component sites carrying the componentwise localized
topologies. This module reads that square at arbitrary topologies equal to them, exactly as
`CategoryTheory.SemiRepresentable.freeYonedaSheafPushforwardPullbackIsoOfEq` reads the isomorphism
itself: that is the shape the simplicial degrees of
`CategoryTheory.SimplicialSemiRepresentable.situation` need, their topology being generated by the
covering families of the simplicial family of sites and only *equal* to the componentwise
localized one.

## Main results

* `CategoryTheory.SemiRepresentable`
  `.shriekRestrictionTransition_comp_freeYonedaSheafPushforwardPullbackIsoOfEq`: **the
  naturality, at any spelling of the two topologies.**

## Implementation notes

The statement lives in its own module rather than beside the square it transports: importing
`SliceAbelianLowerShriekFreeYoneda` into that module puts enough extra instances in scope that the
`isDefEq` checks of the assembly there no longer finish inside a declaration's heartbeat budget.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0D87](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0D87)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0D8B](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0D8B)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite

universe u

namespace CategoryTheory.SemiRepresentable

attribute [local instance] GrothendieckTopology.hasSheafify_addCommGrpCat

variable {C : Type u} [SmallCategory C] (J : GrothendieckTopology C)
  [J.WEqualsLocallyBijective (Type u)] {M N : FormalCoproduct.{u} C} (f : M ⟶ N)

/-- **`j_! j^{-1} ℤ_V^♯ ≅ ℤ_{h_V × F(K)}^♯` is natural in the semi-representable object, at any
spelling of the two componentwise localized topologies.** This is
`shriekRestrictionTransition_comp_freeYonedaSheafPushforwardPullbackIso` with the topologies on
the two component sites taken to be arbitrary ones equal to the componentwise localized
topologies, so that the square can be read at sites whose topologies are presented differently --
which is what the simplicial degrees of
`CategoryTheory.SimplicialSemiRepresentable.situation` are.

The transport is `subst` on the two equalities of topologies: every typeclass the statement needs
is a `Prop`, so the instances carried along by the substitutions and the ones registered at the
componentwise topologies are interchangeable. -/
theorem shriekRestrictionTransition_comp_freeYonedaSheafPushforwardPullbackIsoOfEq
    {Tm : GrothendieckTopology (ComponentOver M)}
    {Tn : GrothendieckTopology (ComponentOver N)}
    [(componentOverForget M).IsContinuous Tm J] [(componentOverForget N).IsContinuous Tn J]
    [(componentOverMap f).IsContinuous Tm Tn]
    (hm : Tm = componentwiseTopology J M) (hn : Tn = componentwiseTopology J N) (V : C) :
    (shriekRestrictionTransition J f Tm Tn AddCommGrpCat.{u}).app
          (Stacks.Cohomology.CohomologyPresheaf.freeYonedaSheaf J V) ≫
        (freeYonedaSheafPushforwardPullbackIsoOfEq J N hn V).hom =
      (freeYonedaSheafPushforwardPullbackIsoOfEq J M hm V).hom ≫
        (presheafToSheaf J AddCommGrpCat.{u}).map
          (Functor.whiskerRight (Limits.prod.map (𝟙 (yoneda.obj V))
            ((FormalCoproduct.yoneda (C := C)).map f)) AddCommGrpCat.free) := by
  subst hm
  subst hn
  exact shriekRestrictionTransition_comp_freeYonedaSheafPushforwardPullbackIso J f V

end CategoryTheory.SemiRepresentable

end
